+					"text": "tele runs scripts: typescript or javascript files in a scripts folder that can call any telegram method, watch every update and change requests on their way. each script is off until you turn it on, and tele asks you, in plain words, before it gets any grant. everything a script can do is in the scripting reference. tele writes typings for every telegram method and type next to your scripts, so editors complete and check them, and a script only gets the grants it declares. scripts can keep their own data on this device and look up the chats and users tele already knows. the mtproto console gets a scripts tab with your scripts and their logs, and an editor that runs code against your account right away. results in the console's script editor unfold like in a browser's devtools, and the editor and its output sit side by side. scripts declare grants like inugram plugins and can hold a request or an update while they decide what to do with it. no script can log in or out, touch your sessions or password, or read login codes. scripts get simple ways to read chats and history, send, edit, delete, forward and react to messages, and to hear about new, edited and deleted ones. scripts can download and upload files, check or rewrite your messages before they go out, and ask you things in tele's own boxes. scripts can add items to the message, chat and profile menus and get a settings page of their own. scripts can add /commands, which show up among the suggestions when you type a slash. scripts can show messages that exist only on this device and never reach telegram. scripts can change how users and chats look on this device: name, color, emoji status, premium star and verification marks. scripts have no limit on menu items, commands, boxes and toasts, and can watch every request with one grant. scripts can put badges and highlights on messages, read messages tele has already loaded, and see the messages you send yourself. scripts can open chats and profiles, read and change the text you're typing, add keyboard shortcuts, and check links and notifications before tele opens or shows them. scripts can add buttons to the chat header and next to the message field, rows to profiles, text fields to their settings pages and buttons to their toasts, and open or save files when you pick them. scripts can post to the notification centre, which gets a scripts tab and a switch for them in its settings. scripts can put badges next to names, add a line under messages, and change a chat's label, preview and badge in the chat list or hide it there. tele → scripts β opens a scripts manager: search, filters, and a page per script with its switch, settings, grants, storage and log. scripts can also read tele's local data and settings, talk to each other, react to the connection and to sleep, and send big files. scripts can recolor the theme, set the window title and badge, control the music player and calls, switch accounts, add items to the main and tray menus, settings sections and quick buttons next to messages, and, if you allow it, run programs. scripts can read and change anything in tele's windows, like adding rows to the gift box, and check inline bot results before they're sent.",
